  "decision_agency": "Borough",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;_Hlk203449671&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;MS Mincho&amp;quot;;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-GB;mso-fareast-language:JA;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;By reason of its\r\ncombined siting, layout, bulk, massing, proximity to boundaries, the proposal\r\nresults in an unsympathetic, cramped and contrived form of overdevelopment that\r\nfails to be in keeping with the character and appearance of the site and\r\nsurrounding to the detriment of the visual amenity of the locality, contrary to\r\nPolicies D3 and D4 of the London Plan and Policy D12.3 of the Local Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;By\r\nreason of the scheme failing to achieve Zero Carbon and the absence of a legal\r\nagreement to secure the required carbon offset fund the scheme fails to provide\r\na sustainable and energy efficient scheme contrary to the aims and objectives\r\nof, in particular, policy CC2.2 of the Merton Local Plan 2024.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;MS Mincho&amp;quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:\r\nJA;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;By reason of combined bulk, mass, height and\r\nproximity to the neighbouring dwellings, the proposed dwelling would result in\r\nan visually obtrusive and dominant form of development to the detriment of the\r\nresidential amenities nearby occupants, in particular, the occupiers of nos.80\r\nand 82 The Drive, by way of loss of outlook, unreasonable sense of enclosure,\r\nloss of daylight and sunlight, overbearing form and loss of privacy contrary\r\nto, in particular, Policy D6 of the London Plan and Policies D12.2, D12.3 and\r\nD12.4 of the Local Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
